<div>
<div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12pt">May 10, 2023<br>
<br>
<br>
City Clerk, City of Winnipeg c/o Appeals Committee<br>
Susan A. Thompson Bldg.<br>
510 Main Street<br>
Winnipeg, MB, R3B 1B9<br>
Fax: 204-947-3452<br>
Email: <a href=3D"mailto:clk-appeals@winnipeg.ca" target=3D"_blank">clk-app=
eals@winnipeg.ca</a><br>
<br>
<br>
RE: City of Winnipeg Variance Ord: DAV 201992/2022C &amp; 10-585 Corydon Av=
enue<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
To whom it may concern,<br>
<br>
I am writing to appeal the variance order listed above. While many city pol=
icies have been adopted to encourage development of residential zoning deve=
lopments, it appears that very little was done to ensure that property regu=
lations and research was properly
 integrated into the planning for this project. We respectfully appeal agai=
nst the approval of the proposed variance application, as it disregards pro=
per procedure and would significantly impact the tenants&#39; ability to en=
joy the services they are entitled to.<br>
<br>
Firstly, it has come to our attention that the Applicant intends to remove =
the community laundry and storage facilities, which are essential services =
provided to the tenants. According to a statement provided by Celena Funk, =
Property Manager of 585 Corydon
 Ave, on May 5, 2023, the Applicant acknowledged that the withdrawal of suc=
h services requires an application to the Residential Tenancies Branch. It =
is concerning that the Applicant has failed to follow this required procedu=
re, raising doubts about the legitimacy
 of their variance application. It is impossible that an application for wi=
thdrawal of services has occurred and been processed by May 11, 2023. As su=
ch, the variance cannot be completed until after review by the Residential =
Tenancies Branch.<br>
<br>
Furthermore, Section 169 of the City of Winnipeg Zoning By-law states that =
a variance application can only be approved if it does not create a substan=
tial adverse effect on the amenities, use, safety, and convenience of the s=
urrounding properties and area.
 It is important to note that the provision of common areas, services, faci=
lities, and privileges, including laundry and storage, is an integral part =
of the rental agreement between the tenants and the landlord. Removing thes=
e services would directly impact
 the tenants&#39; ability to fully enjoy the amenities and conveniences the=
y pay for and are entitled to under their tenancy agreement.<br>
<br>
Additionally, the cost of rent is not solely based on the rental unit itsel=
f but also includes the use of common areas, services, and facilities. If t=
he laundry and storage facilities are removed, it is only fair that the cos=
t of rent be adjusted accordingly
 since these services would no longer be provided. This is not a minor matt=
er, as the removal of these services would have a significant effect on bot=
h the property and the tenants. No alternative has been provided for this t=
enant.<br>
<br>
Considering these factors, we strongly believe that the proposed variance i=
s not desirable and should be rejected. Removing essential services without=
 following the proper procedures not only undermines the rights and expecta=
tions of the tenants, but also raises
 concerns about the Applicant&#39;s compliance with relevant regulations an=
d obligations.<br>
<br>
In light of the above, we kindly request that the Committee carefully consi=
ders the concerns raised in this letter during your evaluation of Thorwin P=
roperties&#39; variance application. We urge you to prioritize the protecti=
on of tenants&#39; rights, the preservation
 of essential services, and the adherence to proper procedures in land deve=
lopment applications.<br>
<br>
Thank you for your attention to this matter. We trust that the Committee wi=
ll act in the best interest of the tenants and the community as a whole. Sh=
ould you require any further information or clarification, please do not he=
sitate to contact me at your earliest
 convenience.<br>
<br>
Sincerely,<br>
Evan Rosner<br>
10-585 Corydon Ave<br>
Winnipeg, MB<br>
R3L0P3<u></u><u></u></p>
